target_text:
// Packed K types (TRON_K_VNNI):
// - k_vnni_tensor holds one bf16 array of [Rows tokens * Cols dimensions]. The
//   array starts at an address that is a multiple of 64 bytes.
// - k_vnni_view refers to that array and computes where each (token, dim) is.
// The view owns no memory. T = bf16 allows writes, and T = const bf16 is
// read-only.

body:
**[comments] Rule 2, restates identifiers: shorten**

The clause "in the K VNNI layout of h/tron/tensor/k_vnni.hpp" restates the name k_vnni and the file pointer the header already gives at lines 5-6, and the "Note [K VNNI storage] in kv_cache.hpp" pointer repeats line 8 of the same file. Dropping both leaves the block in the same shape as the existing Packed V block (lines 28-33), with the facts the forward declarations do not carry: element type bf16, the meaning of Rows and Cols, the 64-byte alignment, and the two allowed values of T.

Proposed:
```cpp
// Packed K types (TRON_K_VNNI):
// - k_vnni_tensor holds one bf16 array of [Rows tokens * Cols dimensions]. The
//   array starts at an address that is a multiple of 64 bytes.
// - k_vnni_view refers to that array and computes where each (token, dim) is.
// The view owns no memory. T = bf16 allows writes, and T = const bf16 is
// read-only.
```
